rms the shaded Netty transport, reactor-netty, and JCTools queues (`io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty...`, `io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools...`) are all bundled *inside* the artifact itself. Nothing to add as a `testImplementation`.\n- **No Docker image needed.** `StatsdConfig` exposes plain `host()`/`port()` methods pointing at a UDP endpoint — tests can bind an ordinary `java.net.DatagramSocket` on localhost/an ephemeral port in-process to capture the emitted packets, exactly like the existing `micrometer-registry-otlp` test in this repo captures exports via an injected in-JVM sender rather than a real collector. No real StatsD/Datadog agent process is required for meaningful coverage.\n- **No env var or system property is required to make the tests reachable.** Everything needed to exercise the registry (config, flavor, protocol) is set programmatically via `StatsdConfig`/`StatsdMeterRegistry.builder(...)`.\n- Interestingly, the jar already ships partial `META-INF/native-image/...` config for `io.netty:*` and `io.projectreactor:*` — confirming the issue's premise: the vendor's bundled config is incomplete for the shaded package names actually used at runtime, which is exactly the kind of gap the normal `generateMetadata` + native-image-agent iteration (fixTestNativeImageRun) workflow is meant to close. That's core metadata-generation work, not a prerequisite \"setup\" step.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"All Netty/reactor-netty/JCTools classes referenced by the issue are shaded inside micrometer-registry-statsd itself (no separate dependency exists to add). Testing needs no Docker StatsD server or env vars — StatsdConfig.host()/port() can point at a local DatagramSocket. The real work is native-image metadata (initialize-at-run-time + reflection) for the shaded classes, which is the normal generation/fix workflow, not extra setup.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Exercise StatsdMeterRegistry with a plain java.net.DatagramSocket bound to localhost on an ephemeral port as the 'StatsD server' (set via StatsdConfig.host()/port()) instead of a real StatsD/Datadog agent or Docker container — the wire protocol is just UDP text lines. Since publishing is async, poll/await the socket receive with a timeout rather than sleeping a fixed duration, and always call registry.close() in a finally block to stop the shaded reactor-netty client and avoid hanging the test JVM. When investigating the reported native-image bug, note the jar already bundles META-INF/native-image config for io.netty/io.projectreactor under their real (unshaded) coordinates — the gap is that the shaded class names (io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.*, io.micrometer.shaded.io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.*) aren't covered, matching the initialize-at-run-time and reflection metadata listed in the issue (DNS resolver holders, epoll/unix transport classes, JCTools MPSC queue field-offset classes). Confirm exact `initialize-at-run-time` needs by running native-image-agent trace plus fixTestNativeImageRun rather than copying the issue's list verbatim, since it was captured against a different Micrometer/Netty pairing (Micronaut, not this repo's harness).\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"The reported failure ('stops publishing after running for a while') is a delayed/lazy class-initialization issue — a short-lived JVM/native-image test run may not trigger it, so coverage should specifically exercise the DNS-resolution and scheduled-task code paths the issue calls out, not just a single metric publish.\",\n    \"Shaded package layout can change between micrometer versions; verify class names against the actual 1.16.5 jar (already done here) rather than assuming the issue's Micronaut-reported list is exhaustive or current.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":13221,"type":"result","duration_ms":105380,"uuid":"e5a90aef-a8d6-4b2c-808b-aaa72939b96a","ttft_stream_ms":1975,"time_to_request_ms":67